# Text RPG

A small terminal RPG written in Python.

This project is primarily a learning project for getting comfortable with Python,
project structure, Git, testing, classes, decorators, and working with a larger
codebase.

The game itself is not the main goal — the main goal is learning by building it.

## Features

- Terminal-based RPG
- Player stats and inventory
- Items and item effects
- Multiple locations
- Roads and random rooms
- Random events
- Merchants
- Combat system
- Different enemy behaviours
- Relics with unique effects
- Save/load system
- Basic automated tests with pytest

## Project structure

├── main.py
├── commands.py
├── combat.py
├── data.py
├── data_file/
│   └── map.py
├── enemies.json
├── events_data.json
├── items.json
├── options.json
├── player_data.json
├── requirements.txt
└── tests/
    └── map_test.py

## Requirements

- pytest

## Installation

pip install -r requirements.txt

## Running the game

python main.py

## Running tests

pytest

##Current state

The project is still in development.

Some systems are unfinished or experimental, and parts of the code are
currently being refactored while I learn better Python practices.

## Why I made this

"I'm using this project to learn how to work with a larger Python project rather than only writing small isolated scripts."

## What I'm learning

Things I'm currently learning include:

-Git
-dependency management with requirements.txt
-automated testing with pytest
-type hints
-decorators
-classes and object-oriented programming
-project structure and refactoring